00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:36.780
Imagine you bought a Canadian industrial name last week after seeing a headline about raised guidance your order filled at the open but the real test comes when the next quarterly report lands

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:43.780
and you must decide whether the beat justifies holding or trimming revenue versus earnings tells the first story.

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:54.360
A company can post higher net income while revenue stalls if it cut costs or used one time gains so always compare year over year revenue growth to the EPS figure.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:08:01.320
Forward guidance and management commentary on the call reveal whether the beat is sustainable or just a timing shift.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:12.080
Check the balance sheet for rising debt alongside declining cash balances free cash flow that diverges sharply from reported earnings often signals working capital strain.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:24.760
Professionals always cross reference the actual EPS beat or miss against the whisper number not just the consensus the misconception to avoid is treating every earnings beat as an automatic buy signal.

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:31.440
Instead read the report for the three metrics above before deciding whether the result changes your original thesis.

